Stream through autoarray's sparse_terms_from_chunks; require 2026.10.2.1

The streamed path's fast accumulation now hands each batch of exactly
NUFFT_BATCH samples to autoarray's own streaming accumulation (released in
2026.10.2.1), which matched pyuvimage's type-1 accumulation to 3e-13 of the
peak on ALMaQUEST CO(1-0) and ran 25% faster on Hannah's Mac. The last
batch is padded with zero-weight (infinite sigma) samples so JAX compiles
one batch length. pyuvimage's own type-1 path remains for the point
components' oversampled grids, for unpooled batches with unequal sigmas
(which autoarray refuses), and as the fallback on an older autoarray,
with a one-time warning giving the pip command.

pyproject: autoarray and autogalaxy >= 2026.10.2.1, replacing the git
head (the release has the solver rewrite the git pin was for). docs/install.md
explains replacing a git-installed autoarray, which reports 9999.0.0.dev0.

From autoarray 2026.10 a sparse inversion's `dataset` is a DatasetInterface
without data arrays; LinearSystem.from_inversion reads data and noise from
the fit's own dataset first. compare_from_stream.py keeps comparing
pyuvimage's own accumulation against from_stream.

